{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Every command invoked through sudo is recorded in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with a timestamp and user details.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sudoers configuration routes sudo events through local2, and rsyslog writes all local2 priorities to the dedicated file. Pre- and post-restart tests show timestamped records containing the invoking user, target user, working directory, and command. The log is root-owned with mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0a72bd549ad4585","cmd-278eee083bfb4400","cmd-9f6abcf716a84c09","cmd-e85ddc1ca5814d1e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The dedicated rsyslog rule stops further processing after writing local2 events. Marker-based tests before and after restart found the sudo events in the dedicated log and zero matches in both /var/log/messages and /var/log/secure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-278eee083bfb4400","cmd-9f6abcf716a84c09","cmd-e85ddc1ca5814d1e"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating and permissioning the two configuration drop-ins was required for the task (cmd-e0a72bd549ad4585); restarting rsyslog and generating bounded test events activated and verified the solution (cmd-278eee083bfb4400); the scheduled reboot fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-6217abd832734bf0); and post-restart sudo invocations were bounded recovery evidence (cmd-e85ddc1ca5814d1e). The restart was fully observed: healthy pre-state and boot ID, acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered system and rsyslog service, retained pre-restart log data, and successful new logging. Lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the boot-ID change, no failed services, unchanged network exposure, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0a72bd549ad4585","cmd-278eee083bfb4400","cmd-9f6abcf716a84c09","cmd-6217abd832734bf0","cmd-51929545a7d547f4","cmd-e85ddc1ca5814d1e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence before and after restart. The dedicated sudo log records the required command, user, and timestamp information, while tested entries are excluded from the general log files. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete and consistent with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
